-- title:
--   Reduction-linear relations are respected by admissible readings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ belongs to `A.nonunits`. Let $\kappa_A$ denote the residue field of $A$ and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` datum for the field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F$, the base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` inside Laurent series, with target `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of $\kappa_A$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`; thus $R_0$ consists of a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto that target whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which extends the residue map of $A$ on constants, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders. Assume $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficients lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a subring of the rational Laurent series whose members are exactly the $gf$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficient image lies in `R₀.integers` and which satisfy $\mathrm{ord}_P(gf) \ge 0$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $\mathrm{ord}_P(jq) \ge 0$; assume $jq \in \mathcal{A}$. Let $\Omega$ be a field with a $\kappa_A$-algebra structure and $\mathrm{val} : \mathcal{A} \to \Omega$ a ring homomorphism which vanishes on every element of $\mathcal{A}$ whose $R_0$-residue is $0$, and such that $\mathrm{val}(jq)$ is transcendental over $\kappa_A$. Then for every $n$, every family $gf_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n$) of rational Laurent series lying in $\mathcal{A}$, in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficient images in `R₀.integers`, and all coefficients $c_i \in \kappa_A$: if $\sum_i c_i \cdot R_0(\overline{gf_i}) = 0$ in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, then $\sum_i \mathrm{image}_\Omega(c_i)\,\mathrm{val}(gf_i) = 0$ in $\Omega$.
--
--   This transfers $\kappa_A$-linear relations among the reductions of admissible rational level-$M'$ functions to the corresponding relations among their images under any reading $\mathrm{val}$ that kills the functions of zero reduction, the transcendence of $\mathrm{val}(jq)$ playing the role of a generic point. It is the linear-algebra input to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_of_ringHom_admissible_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_of_ringHom_admissible_of_prime), which upgrades such a reading to an algebra homomorphism on the reduced full-level function field; unlike related statements in this circle it assumes only that $q$ is prime and prime to $M'$, with no lower bound on $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_sum_algebraMap_mul_apply_eq_zero_of_sum_smul_residue_eq_zero_of_prime.lean

